{"content":[{"c":["MISREPHOTH-MAIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["One of the northernmost places to which the Israelites pursued the fleeing Canaanite armies defeated at the waters of Merom (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.8","r":"Josh.11.8","rawR":"Josh.11.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.8","value":"Josh.11.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:8"},"). Misrephoth-maim, meaning “burning of water,” defined part of the boundary of land remaining yet to be possessed by Israel during the days of Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.6","r":"Josh.13.6","rawR":"Josh.13.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.6","value":"Josh.13.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:6"},"). In all probability, Misrephoth-maim is identical with the cluster of springs at Khirbet el-Musheirifeh near the Mediterranean Sea, 20 miles (32.2 kilometers) south of Sidon and 6 miles (9.7 kilometers) north of Tyre, at the base of Ras en-Nakurah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MisrephothMaim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 11:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.8","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.8","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.8"},{"anchorText":"13:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.6","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.6","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cb099898786329e9890e1c18d01d612895170bbf482706874a1c00e38962edd4","sourceItemName":"MisrephothMaim","sourceItemOrder":361,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"MisrephothMaim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Misrephoth-Maim","title":"Misrephoth-Maim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}